    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Use shared decision-making to choose monotherapy for uncomplicated major depression; patient prefers medication over psychotherapy. Guideline: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Major Depressive Disorder (2022) [S]</item><item>Start sertraline 50 mg daily; review expected time to benefit, common adverse effects, and how to reach the clinic. Guideline: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Major Depressive Disorder (2022) [S]</item><item>Repeat PHQ-9 at six and twelve weeks and adjust treatment if response is inadequate; plan continuation treatment after remission. Guideline: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Major Depressive Disorder (2022) [S]</item><item>Create a collaborative safety plan with crisis resources, including the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline. Guideline: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024) [S]</item><item>Psychiatry consultation to confirm the diagnosis and advise on medication management. Guideline: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Major Depressive Disorder (2022) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
